window.EXHIBITION.introduction=["Students in CHLA 215 \"Introduction to the Medical Humanities\" developed these projects in 2025 and 2026. Together, they approach medicine as an ethical, social, political, and lived practice.", "Through research, oral history, documentary film, sound, images, and personal reflection, they examine care amid war and overlapping crises in contemporary Lebanon. They explore how war injures bodies, disrupts care, and leaves traces in memory long after the moment of violence. These works form an emerging archive: its histories and questions remain open.", "Watch, listen, read, and look closely. Scroll at your own pace, or enter through any individual work."];
